       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is above the safe limit.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 2000 mg three times daily is 6,000 mg/day. The usual adult maximum is 4,000 mg/day, and some institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 2000 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** At 6 g/day there is a real risk of hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nHere are some options:\n1. **1000 mg by mouth three times daily** (3,000 mg/day). This is a common conservative regimen.\n2. **1000 mg by mouth four times daily** (4,000 mg/day). This is the standard maximum.\n3. **650 mg by mouth every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day).\n\nIf you meant 2000 mg/day total, or a different dose or frequency, tell me and I'll enter it. If you do want 2000 mg three times daily, please confirm that it's intentional and give the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
